Column H holds elapsed time as a fraction of a day (`C3-$C$2`), while column I holds a seconds grid (0, 0.5, 1, …). Multiplying H by 86400 converts it to seconds, which gives a value in J2 you can compare directly with column I.

{"formula": "=H2*86400"}

The cell M2 sits above M3 and M4, which already hold the same pattern, so the formula for M2 should follow it with the row reference changed to $H2.

